# Git commit and push

Remote: `git@github.com:shemaiahCox/langchain-sql-agent.git` (`origin`).

Commit only when the user explicitly asks. Push only when the user explicitly asks. Do not update git config, skip hooks, or force-push `main`.

Never stage `.env`, credentials, `.venv/`, or `__pycache__/`.

## Commit

```bash
git status
git diff
git log -5 --oneline

git add <relevant-files>
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Short message focused on why.

EOF
)"
git status
```

If a hook rejects the commit, fix the problem and make a new commit. Do not amend unless the user asked and the commit is unpushed and was created in this conversation.

## Push

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
```

Use `git push` when the branch already tracks `origin`. Do not force-push.
